alright so you probably think that i'm  completely nuts because of that title  but there's a very real chance that  apple could be ditching  the 11-inch ipad pro for next year's  update and instead just releasing  a larger more expensive 12.9 inch ipad  pro model  with a bunch of huge upgrades so what  i'm gonna do in this video is go through  a bunch of leaks  that point to this actually being a  possibility  and then i'm gonna talk about why it  actually makes sense  for apple to ditch the 11 ipad pro model  and then i'll finish off by discussing  some of the features that we should  expect in  the 12.9 inch ipad pro and one we should  realistically  expected to be released so let's get  started with some of the leaks that go  all the way back  to december of 2019 when ming chaqua  said that a new  12.9 inch ipad pro with a mini led  display  would be coming in the second half of  2020  and then in march of 2020 ming added  more apple devices to the list of  products  getting mini led displays later that  year  that obviously didn't happen because  kovid 19  caused massive delays pushing back all  of the mini led device rumors  into 2021. now what's interesting about  all of those rumors  is that the 11 inch ipad pro is nowhere  to be seen  which is really odd because apple has  recently been updating both  sizes at the same time and then once  again  in september he released another note  yet again ignoring the 11 inch model and  most recently just a couple of days ago  he mentioned that the 12.9 inch ipad pro  with a mini led display  will launch in the first quarter of 2021  but yet again no mention of the 11 inch  this instantly caused multiple mac  rumors users  to suspect that apple is in fact not  releasing an 11 inch ipad pro  alongside the new 12.9 inch model next  year  i also saw a couple of reddit posts with  users wondering the same thing  will apple discontinue the 11 inch ipad  pro  and just keep the larger 12.9 inch model  well i did a bit more digging and found  some very interesting leaks  fudge a leaker with over 90 accuracy  said on june 2nd that ipad pros with an  a14x chip will be coming  basically pointing at two different  sizes right after that  love to dream with an 89 accuracy rating  retweeted  fudge's tweet and added that they'll get  a mini led display  and a 5g modem and then he retweeted  again  stating that they're coming either in  the first or second quarter of 2021  but one thing to note is that he didn't  correct fudge  in terms of whether there will be two or  just one ipad pro model  so in reality there's a chance that the  11 inch ipad pro could be sticking  around  maybe we'll only see a 12.9 inch ipad  pro in march  and then maybe later in 2021 apple will  update the 11 inch model but i  personally find it a bit hard to believe  that they'd split up the release dates  unless they make some major changes  in my personal opinion if apple does end  up  only releasing a 12.9 inch ipad pro in  march  then the 11 inch is dead for good but in  that case  they could be planning to update the  ipad pro at a later date  with a larger display potentially an  11.5 inch display instead of 11.  this would allow them to raise the base  price especially if they add more  features  this would also allow them to create a  larger magic keyboard case  with a more comfortable keyboard instead  of the current  scrunch down version they might even  release the second generation of the  magic keyboard  alongside that new 11.5 inch ipad pro  model  which will further boost sales of that  new ipad pro  on top of that if apple releases only  one  12.9 inch ipad pro in march this would  allow apple to make a lot of money  thanks to the higher base price of 999  dollars  and the massive wave of hype due to it  being the first apple product  to come with a mini led display and also  thanks to the super powerful  a14x chip which i'll get into in just a  second  essentially a lot of people will be  upgrading to this new ipad pro  even if they would have preferred a  smaller 11 inch display  and then at a later date maybe even a  year and a half later  apple would release the 11.5 inch ipad  pro  allowing them to bump up the base price  of that model  now with all of that out of the way i  want to talk about the other reason  why it would actually make sense for  apple to ditch  the 11-inch ipad pro the number one  reason is because apple's new ipad air 4  is extremely similar to the 11-inch ipad  pro  from the front you can't even tell them  apart  and on the back the only noticeable  difference is  the camera bump because of that apple  desperately tried to make the pro  seem better than the air they even went  as far as making the air's display  10.9 inches to make the 11 inch pro seem  just a bit better  they even invested hugely into putting  touch id into the power button  instead of simply giving it face id  which would have been  a less expensive option the ipad air has  4 speaker grilles  but they only put in 2 speakers just to  make the pro  seem better with its quad speakers it's  completely obvious that apple tried very  hard  to make the pro seem more premium and  even still  many users are going for the new ipad  air 4  because it looks basically the same and  the performance is  almost on par because of that it totally  makes sense for apple to ditch the 11  inch ipad pro  and come back stronger with a new 11.5  inch or larger model  with new features and upgrades so that  they can bump up the base price  and that would definitely help  differentiate the  air and the pro and make the whole ipad  lineup  make a lot more sense now i want to  finally get into the 12.9 inch model  and what we should expect from it first  off it's rumored to be the very first  apple product  to come with the new mini led display  and that alone will generate massive  hype and extra sales  if you're not familiar with mini led  technology it basically works  like apple's pro display xdr instead of  having one large led backlight  like all of apple's current ipad and mac  displays use  mini led uses hundreds or thousands of  leds  that light up locally controlled dimming  zones  to offer excellent contrast and colors  similar to an oled display  but without all of its drawbacks many  led displays  actually still use lcd panels so there  will be no burn-in issues  like oleds have and there won't be any  flickering issues  that give some people headaches so  basically  when you watch a movie or video on your  ipad the black bars at the top and  bottom  will actually be black and not gray like  they currently are  and that will actually cause it to save  battery life as well  now moving on to the other features we  can expect the main one  is the a14x chip i've seen a lot of  people claim that the new ipad pro  will come with the m1 chip but that is  dead wrong the m series of chips are  meant to be  exclusive to the mac hence the m  those mac socs come with extra chips  like the i o controller  the thunderbolt controller chips up to  16 gigs of soldered on ram  and other mac related things that the  ipad  simply doesn't need because it only  needs to run the more simple  ipad os software it'll instead come with  the a14x chip  which will basically be a stripped-down  version of the m1  only containing what it needs like the  a-core cpu  the a-core gpu the 16-core neural engine  and other things like the ram and video  encoders  because of that it's going to have  performance similar to the fanless m1  macbook air  but probably a bit worse because the  ipad pro's chassis  is quite a lot thinner than the macbook  air so it's not going to be able to  dissipate heat as well  but nevertheless the performance is  going to be absolutely insane for a  tablet  and there's actually a chance that we  could be seeing apple bring  pro apps like final cut pro over to the  ipad  starting with ipad os 15. and this  actually makes sense  since apple has recently updated those  pro apps  to support apple silicon so it should  technically be able to work on the ipad  with some minor tweaks now as far as  some of the other features  there is a chance that apple could  upgrade the face id sensor  to work better and be smaller  potentially allowing apple  to slim down the bezels by a bit and  with that apple could introduce  multi-user support  which was recently rumored to be coming  soon and it would work  perfectly thanks to face id on the ipad  pro  and touch id on all of the other ipad  models  but other than all of that i don't think  that we should expect apple to change  much else on the 12.9 inch ipad pro  but the one feature i would absolutely  love to see  would be for apple to move the webcam  from the top  to the side so that web conferencing  looks  normal when using the magic keyboard  case so there you guys have it there are  all of my thoughts on the 12.9 inch ipad  pro  and why we could potentially see apple  ditch the 11 inch ipad pro model  if you disagree with me go ahead and  comment below and if you enjoyed this  video tap the like button  click the circle about to subscribe for  more videos like this one  definitely check out one of those two  videos right over there and we'll see  you in the next video  [Music]

